<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n52456" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάκ-ωσις</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κᾰκόω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ill-treatment</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ ἡγεμόνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					4.6.3
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stud.Pal.</u>
				1.8.10
			</span></i> (V <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
			</span></i>); <i>oppression</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ λαοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Ex.</u>
					3.7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> esp. in Law,
				<i>ill-usage</i>, of persons by their natural protectors, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ τῆς κ. νόμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					13.91
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Is.
				8.32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				10.40
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γραφὴ κακώσεως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					58.32
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				328
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. γονέων, ὀρφανῶν, ἐπικλήρου,
				οἴκου ὀρφανικοῦ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ath.</u>
				56.6
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοκέων κ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Lycurg.
				147
			</span></i>; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἐπαρχίας</span>
			<i>misgovernment</i>, of the Rom. <i>actio repetundarum</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Caes.</u>
				4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>suffering, distress</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.43
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πληρωμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					7.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰκίαι σωμάτων καὶ κακώσεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1386a8
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1385a24
			</span></i>; of the effects of disease, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>VM</u>
				17
			</span></i>: pl., Id.<i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				19
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ τᾶς σαρκὸς τακομένας κακώσιες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ti.Locr.
					102c
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mort.</u>
				21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.31
			</span></i>.</div>
